---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Work — Gonzalo Ferrero Martín"
  description="What I have built, with the checks behind it: a DVI transmitter in Verilog, a HiFi player, an autonomous rover, a four-board cradle and five smaller builds."
  kind="work-index"
  depth={1}
  ground="paper"
>
<main id="main">

  <section class="page cs">
    <p class="kicker col-head">4 case studies · 5 smaller builds · <span class="nb">2025 – present</span></p>
    <h1 class="col-head">Work</h1>
    <p class="deck col-prose">Everything I have built so far, with the checks behind it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="page sec" id="projects">
    <hr class="sec__rule col-full">
    <p class="sec__reading col-margin">4 projects · 2 in progress</p>
    <h2 class="col-head">Case studies</h2>

    <article class="row col-full" id="hdmi">
      <p class="row__no">01</p>
      <div class="row__title">
        <h3><a href="hdmi-dvi-transmitter.html">HDMI / DVI transmitter</a></h3>
        <p class="row__deck">A DVI video pipeline in Verilog: timing, pattern, TMDS encoder; serializer in progress.</p>
        <p class="row__notice"><span class="mono">decode(encode(d)) == d</span> on every symbol, against an independent decoder.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="row__meta">
        <li>Verilog · XSIM · PYNQ-Z2</li>
        <li><span class="nb">Jul 2026 – present</span></li>
        <li><span class="status">in progress</span></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="row col-full" id="venus">
      <p class="row__no">02</p>
      <div class="row__title">
        <h3><a href="venus-rover.html">Venus rover</a></h3>
        <p class="row__deck">Run-on-boot C firmware for a PYNQ-Z2 rover that hunts colored cubes and coordinates with a partner over MQTT.</p>
        <p class="row__notice">Cubes confirmed by a 6-read burst vote, <span class="nb">≥2 within 5 cm</span>.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="row__meta">
        <li>C · Python · PYNQ-Z2 · ESP32</li>
        <li>TU/e 5EID0 · 2026</li>
        <li>complete</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="row col-full" id="hifi">
      <p class="row__no">03</p>
      <div class="row__title">
        <h3><a href="hifi-player.html">Battery-powered HiFi player</a></h3>
        <p class="row__deck">Schematic, 4-layer PCB, power path and ESP32-S3R8 firmware; Bluetooth or microSD into an I2S DAC.</p>
        <p class="row__notice">Designed end to end; nothing bench-verified yet.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="row__meta">
        <li>PCB layout · C · ESP32-S3R8</li>
        <li><span class="nb">May 2026 – present</span></li>
        <li><span class="status">in progress</span></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="row col-full" id="ryb">
      <p class="row__no">04</p>
      <div class="row__title">
        <h3><a href="rock-your-baby.html">Rock Your Baby</a></h3>
        <p class="row__deck">A distributed baby-monitoring cradle: four PYNQ-Z2 subsystems over UART.</p>
        <p class="row__notice">RMS with noise-floor subtraction on a pthread capture loop.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="row__meta">
        <li>C · libpynq · PYNQ-Z2</li>
        <li>TU/e 5EWC0 · <span class="nb">2025 – 26</span></li>
        <li>complete</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="page sec" id="builds">
    <hr class="sec__rule col-full">
    <p class="sec__reading col-margin">5 builds · 1 in progress</p>
    <h2 class="col-head">Smaller builds</h2>
    <ul class="nlist col-a">
      <li id="counter">
        <p class="nlist__kicker">Verilog · 5EIC0</p>
        <h3 class="nlist__title">32-bit counter from gate logic</h3>
        <p>Half-adders from an XOR and an AND, full-adders from two half-adders, a 32-bit ripple adder from <span class="nb">32</span> of those, and a clocked counter with enable and reset on top, interfaced to an AXI4-Lite bus so a processor can configure it. Simulated, then run on the PYNQ board.</p>
      </li>
      <li id="edurv">
        <p class="nlist__kicker">Verilog · C · 5EIC0</p>
        <h3 class="nlist__title">EduRV RISC-V labs</h3>
        <p>Labs on EduRV, an educational RISC-V core: simulating it in Verilator, working with it in Vivado, and writing C code that runs on the core itself.</p>
      </li>
      <li id="i2c">
        <p class="nlist__kicker">Verilog · <span class="status">in progress</span></p>
        <h3 class="nlist__title">I²C master</h3>
        <p>A reusable configuration block for the HDMI transmitter — reading the sink’s EDID over DDC — and, later, an audio DAC. So far only the module interface exists: address, data and an enable strobe in; SCL and a bidirectional SDA out. Body and testbench still to be written.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="nlist col-b">
      <li id="plotter">
        <p class="nlist__kicker">C · <span class="nc">libpynq</span></p>
        <h3 class="nlist__title">Function plotter</h3>
        <p>An oscilloscope-style plotter that draws equations, with axes, on the <span class="nb">240×240</span> TFT: sine and cosine, alone or together, from 360-entry lookup tables, scaled by an adjustable ratio.</p>
      </li>
      <li id="snake">
        <p class="nlist__kicker">C · <span class="nc">libpynq</span></p>
        <h3 class="nlist__title">Snake</h3>
        <p>A tick-based game loop: the snake moves every <span class="nb">200 ms</span>, but the loop polls the buttons every <span class="nb">10 ms</span>, keeps the last valid direction and rejects a <span class="nb">180°</span> reversal, so input feels instant.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

</main>
</Base>
